    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0385" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890g.6363 T 84/124: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Bagdad</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Randolph</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bagdad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-12-15T12:00:00+03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 15,
                                1923—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received December 16—5:25
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>In reply to Department’s telegram December 13, 6 p.m.<anchor n="51"
                        xml:id="d163-f1"/> Petroleum negotiations were progressing, agreement
                    reached on all except a few [un]important matters when the fall of the old
                    Cabinet November 16th necessitated commencing negotiations from the beginning
                    with new Cabinet which has formed committee of three (Ministers Justice,
                    Interior, and Works) to negotiate with Keeling and first meeting will be held
                    tomorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Randolph</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
